/A 1932 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart diagram depicting two main phases: \(a\) Training phase involves feeding RGB observation through a foveated visual encoder, sampling timestep and noise, adding noise to demonstration action, predicting noise via a conditional noise predictor using cross-attention and minimizing mean squared error loss. \(b\) Inference phase starts from noise, applies DDIM scheduler and iterative denoising via the same conditional noise predictor with cross-attention, producing final prediction, unnormalizing it to executable robot actions and optionally engaging closed-loop control. Solid and dashed arrows indicate data flow and conditioning injection. Legends define action chunk, noise action, Gaussian noise, visual conditioning, and diffusion step.)
/ID (ID.00662)
/K 1933 0 R
/P 1600 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
