/Alt (Three-panel figure. Panel \(a\) is a flow diagram labeled "End-to-end control cycle boundary" showing modules: image acquisition, object detection/box tracking, FDP policy inference, communication/low-level control, and robot actuation/environment; dashed modules are excluded from reported latency. Panel \(b\) describes "Inside FDP policy inference," detailing a process of dual-stream visual encoding, DDIM denoising loop, and action chunk output, highlighting repeated computation. Panel \(c\) is a line chart labeled "DDIM steps vs. policy-level latency," showing that increasing DDIM sampling steps raises policy-level latency, with a default point marked at 10 steps, 55 milliseconds, and 18.2 FPS.)
/ID (ID.00851)
/K 2882 0 R
/P 1600 0 R
